<div class="credit-caption">
    <div class="caption-wrap">
        <div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption">
            <p>
                A man documents destroyed buildings at the site of an Israeli airstrike in Beirut's southern suburb, Lebanon, on Tuesday.
                <b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit">

                    Hassan Ammar/AP

                </b>
                <b class="hide-caption"><b>hide caption</b></b>
            </p>
        </div>


            <b class="toggle-caption"><b>toggle caption</b></b>
    </div>

    <span class="credit" aria-label="Image credit">

        Hassan Ammar/AP

    </span>
</div>
   </div>
   <p>Lebanese politicians urgently called on the international community to pressure Israel to stop its advance into Lebanese territory on Tuesday, as Israeli troops crossed into southern Lebanon in an operation targeting Hezbollah outposts.</p>   <p>Lebanon’s caretaker prime minister, Najib Mikati, warned on Tuesday that his country was facing “one of the most dangerous phases of its history,” urging the United Nations for emergency funding for civilians impacted by the conflict.</p>   <div id="resnx-s1-5134606-100" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col ">
            <div class="bucket img">
                  <a class="imagewrap" id="featuredStackSquareImageg-s1-25657" href="https://www.npr.org/2024/10/01/g-s1-25657/israel-ground-offensive-lebanon"  data-metrics-ga4='{"category":"recirculation","action":"story_recirculation_click","clickType":"inset box","clickUrl":"https:\/\/www.npr.org\/2024\/10\/01\/g-s1-25657\/israel-ground-offensive-lebanon"}' ><picture><source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3849x3849+963+0/resize/100/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fef%2F652fc4b34c5a85e998b426969c0d%2Fnpr-north-edit-1.jpg" data-original="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3849x3849+963+0/resize/100/quality/100/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fef%2F652fc4b34c5a85e998b426969c0d%2Fnpr-north-edit-1.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3849x3849+963+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fef%2F652fc4b34c5a85e998b426969c0d%2Fnpr-north-edit-1.jpg" data-format="webp" class="img lazyOnLoad" type="image/webp" /><source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3849x3849+963+0/resize/100/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fef%2F652fc4b34c5a85e998b426969c0d%2Fnpr-north-edit-1.jpg" data-original="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3849x3849+963+0/resize/100/quality/100/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fef%2F652fc4b34c5a85e998b426969c0d%2Fnpr-north-edit-1.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3849x3849+963+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fef%2F652fc4b34c5a85e998b426969c0d%2Fnpr-north-edit-1.jpg" data-format="jpeg" class="img lazyOnLoad" type="image/jpeg" /><img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3849x3849+963+0/resize/100/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fef%2F652fc4b34c5a85e998b426969c0d%2Fnpr-north-edit-1.jpg" data-original="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3849x3849+963+0/resize/100/quality/100/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fef%2F652fc4b34c5a85e998b426969c0d%2Fnpr-north-edit-1.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3849x3849+963+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fef%2F652fc4b34c5a85e998b426969c0d%2Fnpr-north-edit-1.jpg" data-format="jpeg" class="img lazyOnLoad" alt="Tanks and troops gather in northern Israel on Monday in preparation for a ground invasion." loading="lazy" /></picture></a>         <div class="bucketblock">
                        <h3 class="slug"><a href="https://www.npr.org/series/1205445976/middle-east-crisis">Middle East conflict </a></h3>
            <h3><a href="https://www.npr.org/2024/10/01/g-s1-25657/israel-ground-offensive-lebanon"  data-metrics-ga4='{"category":"recirculation","action":"story_recirculation_click","clickType":"inset box","clickUrl":"https:\/\/www.npr.org\/2024\/10\/01\/g-s1-25657\/israel-ground-offensive-lebanon"}' >Israel begins ground offensive in Lebanon</a></h3>
         </div>

<!-- END CLASS="BUCKETBLOCK" -->
      </div>

<!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" -->
   </div>

<!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-5134606-100" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " -->
   <p>Imran Riza, the U.N’s deputy special coordinator in Lebanon, said the country was <a href="https://x.com/Imran_Riza/status/1841064253865771064">seeking $426 million</a> in U.N. assistance.</p>   <p>“As violence escalates, we call on the global community to provide this much needed support and to ensure protection of civilians,” Riza said. “Without sufficient resources, humanitarians risk leaving the population of an entire country without the support they urgently require.”</p>   <aside id="ad-backstage-wrap" class="ad-wrap backstage" aria-label="advertisement">
    <div class="ad-header "><span>Sponsor Message</span></div>

    <div class="ad-config-wrap">
      <div id="ad-backstage-News_World_Middle_East" class="ad-config ad-backstage has-refresh-enabled" data-ad-config='{"network":"\/6735\/","zone":"News_World_Middle_East","targets":{"testserver":"false","isPodcastEpisode":"false","storyId":"nx-s1-5134606","agg":["1205445976","1046346178"]},"site":{"desktop":"n6735.NPR","mobile":"n6735.NPRMOBILE"},"location":"backstage","deferred":false,"isBetweenContent":true,"hasRefreshEnabled":true,"isOutstreamVideoEnabled":true}'>
        <div style="min-height:90px"></div>
      </div>
    </div>


    <div class="ad-footer "></div>
</aside>
   <div id="resnx-s1-5134606-101" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col ">
            <div class="bucket img">
                  <a class="imagewrap" id="featuredStackSquareImageg-s1-25707" href="https://www.npr.org/2024/10/01/g-s1-25707/iran-israel-hezbollah-lebanon-attack"  data-metrics-ga4='{"category":"recirculation","action":"story_recirculation_click","clickType":"inset box","clickUrl":"https:\/\/www.npr.org\/2024\/10\/01\/g-s1-25707\/iran-israel-hezbollah-lebanon-attack"}' ><picture><source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5535x5535+1495+0/resize/100/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa0%2F83%2F40e13d324e339a5ae898acf608e0%2Firan-rocket-barrage-edit-3.jpg" data-original="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5535x5535+1495+0/resize/100/quality/100/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa0%2F83%2F40e13d324e339a5ae898acf608e0%2Firan-rocket-barrage-edit-3.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5535x5535+1495+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa0%2F83%2F40e13d324e339a5ae898acf608e0%2Firan-rocket-barrage-edit-3.jpg" data-format="webp" class="img lazyOnLoad" type="image/webp" /><source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5535x5535+1495+0/resize/100/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa0%2F83%2F40e13d324e339a5ae898acf608e0%2Firan-rocket-barrage-edit-3.jpg" data-original="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5535x5535+1495+0/resize/100/quality/100/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa0%2F83%2F40e13d324e339a5ae898acf608e0%2Firan-rocket-barrage-edit-3.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5535x5535+1495+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa0%2F83%2F40e13d324e339a5ae898acf608e0%2Firan-rocket-barrage-edit-3.jpg" data-format="jpeg" class="img lazyOnLoad" type="image/jpeg" /><img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5535x5535+1495+0/resize/100/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa0%2F83%2F40e13d324e339a5ae898acf608e0%2Firan-rocket-barrage-edit-3.jpg" data-original="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5535x5535+1495+0/resize/100/quality/100/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa0%2F83%2F40e13d324e339a5ae898acf608e0%2Firan-rocket-barrage-edit-3.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5535x5535+1495+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa0%2F83%2F40e13d324e339a5ae898acf608e0%2Firan-rocket-barrage-edit-3.jpg" data-format="jpeg" class="img lazyOnLoad" alt="In this photo, several Israelis lie face down on the ground beside a highway, taking shelter during a massive missile barrage from Iran on October 1, 2024." loading="lazy" /></picture></a>         <div class="bucketblock">
                        <h3 class="slug"><a href="https://www.npr.org/series/1205445976/middle-east-crisis">Middle East conflict </a></h3>
            <h3><a href="https://www.npr.org/2024/10/01/g-s1-25707/iran-israel-hezbollah-lebanon-attack"  data-metrics-ga4='{"category":"recirculation","action":"story_recirculation_click","clickType":"inset box","clickUrl":"https:\/\/www.npr.org\/2024\/10\/01\/g-s1-25707\/iran-israel-hezbollah-lebanon-attack"}' >Iran carries out a massive missile attack on Israel, expanding the Middle East conflict</a></h3>
         </div>

<!-- END CLASS="BUCKETBLOCK" -->
      </div>

<!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" -->
   </div>

<!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-5134606-101" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " -->
   <p>Israeli airstrikes have killed more than 1,000 people in Lebanon over the last two weeks, according to Lebanon’s Health Ministry. The U.N. says <a href="https://news.un.org/en/story/2024/10/1155186">around 1 million people</a> — nearly a fifth of the country — have been displaced from their homes while fleeing this bombardment.</p>   <p>Israel’s offensive follows <a href="https://www.npr.org/2024/09/29/g-s1-25348/israel-hezbollah-lebanon-hassan-nasrallah-timeline" target="g-s1-25348">days of intensifying fighting</a> between Israel and Hezbollah, an Iran-backed Lebanese militant group.</p>   <div id="resnx-s1-5134606-102" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col ">
            <div class="bucket img">
                  <a class="imagewrap" id="featuredStackSquareImageg-s1-25348" href="https://www.npr.org/2024/09/29/g-s1-25348/israel-hezbollah-lebanon-hassan-nasrallah-timeline"  data-metrics-ga4='{"category":"recirculation","action":"story_recirculation_click","clickType":"inset box","clickUrl":"https:\/\/www.npr.org\/2024\/09\/29\/g-s1-25348\/israel-hezbollah-lebanon-hassan-nasrallah-timeline"}' ><picture><source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3648x3648+912+0/resize/100/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F79%2F8d%2F20ef19e74be789977e33a93175da%2Fgettyimages-2173686267.jpg" data-original="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3648x3648+912+0/resize/100/quality/100/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F79%2F8d%2F20ef19e74be789977e33a93175da%2Fgettyimages-2173686267.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3648x3648+912+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F79%2F8d%2F20ef19e74be789977e33a93175da%2Fgettyimages-2173686267.jpg" data-format="webp" class="img lazyOnLoad" type="image/webp" /><source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3648x3648+912+0/resize/100/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F79%2F8d%2F20ef19e74be789977e33a93175da%2Fgettyimages-2173686267.jpg" data-original="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3648x3648+912+0/resize/100/quality/100/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F79%2F8d%2F20ef19e74be789977e33a93175da%2Fgettyimages-2173686267.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3648x3648+912+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F79%2F8d%2F20ef19e74be789977e33a93175da%2Fgettyimages-2173686267.jpg" data-format="jpeg" class="img lazyOnLoad" type="image/jpeg" /><img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3648x3648+912+0/resize/100/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F79%2F8d%2F20ef19e74be789977e33a93175da%2Fgettyimages-2173686267.jpg" data-original="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3648x3648+912+0/resize/100/quality/100/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F79%2F8d%2F20ef19e74be789977e33a93175da%2Fgettyimages-2173686267.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3648x3648+912+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F79%2F8d%2F20ef19e74be789977e33a93175da%2Fgettyimages-2173686267.jpg" data-format="jpeg" class="img lazyOnLoad" alt="A portrait of Hezbollah chief Hassan Nasrallah sits amid destruction in a area targeted overnight by Israeli airstrikes in Saksakiyeh on Sep. 26, 2024." loading="lazy" /></picture></a>         <div class="bucketblock">
                        <h3 class="slug"><a href="https://www.npr.org/series/1205445976/middle-east-crisis">Middle East conflict </a></h3>
            <h3><a href="https://www.npr.org/2024/09/29/g-s1-25348/israel-hezbollah-lebanon-hassan-nasrallah-timeline"  data-metrics-ga4='{"category":"recirculation","action":"story_recirculation_click","clickType":"inset box","clickUrl":"https:\/\/www.npr.org\/2024\/09\/29\/g-s1-25348\/israel-hezbollah-lebanon-hassan-nasrallah-timeline"}' >From pager blasts to Nasrallah’s killing: 12 days that transformed a bloody conflict</a></h3>
         </div>

<!-- END CLASS="BUCKETBLOCK" -->
      </div>

<!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" -->
   </div>

<!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-5134606-102" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " -->
   <p>The conflict entered a dramatic new phase over the weekend, following Israel’s killing of Hezbollah’s longtime leader Hassan Nasrallah, as well as several other top officials.</p>   <div id="resnx-s1-5134606-103" class="bucketwrap statichtml">
            <div style="max-width: 650px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">

<p data-pym-loader data-child-src="https://apps.npr.org/datawrapper/WhH6c/2/" id="responsive-embed-WhH6c">Loading...</p>
<script src="https://pym.nprapps.org/npr-pym-loader.v2.min.js"></script>

</div>
   </div>

<!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-5134606-103" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP STATICHTML" -->
   <p>And now Israel says it is running a “limited” incursion of “targeted ground raids” in southern Lebanon aimed at Hezbollah militants that pose a threat to communities in northern Israel. Israeli authorities say about 63,000 Israelis remain displaced from the border area with Lebanon due to Hezbollah rocket fire.</p>   <div id="resnx-s1-5134606-104" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col ">
            <div class="bucket img">
                  <a class="imagewrap" id="featuredStackSquareImage1208680784" href="https://www.npr.org/2023/10/26/1208680784/death-toll-in-gaza-approaches-7-000-as-aid-groups-raise-alarm-about-fuel"  data-metrics-ga4='{"category":"recirculation","action":"story_recirculation_click","clickType":"inset box","clickUrl":"https:\/\/www.npr.org\/2023\/10\/26\/1208680784\/death-toll-in-gaza-approaches-7-000-as-aid-groups-raise-alarm-about-fuel"}' ><picture><source srcset="https://media.npr.org/assets/img/2023/10/26/gettyimages-1746298515_sq-6d71bd2abe2eba2a3e85ec794b550d5321f1eefa.jpg?s=100&c=85&f=jpeg" data-original="https://media.npr.org/assets/img/2023/10/26/gettyimages-1746298515_sq-6d71bd2abe2eba2a3e85ec794b550d5321f1eefa.jpg?s=100&c=100&f=jpeg" data-template="https://media.npr.org/assets/img/2023/10/26/gettyimages-1746298515_sq-6d71bd2abe2eba2a3e85ec794b550d5321f1eefa.jpg?s={width}&c={quality}&f={format}" data-format="webp" class="img lazyOnLoad" type="image/webp" /><source srcset="https://media.npr.org/assets/img/2023/10/26/gettyimages-1746298515_sq-6d71bd2abe2eba2a3e85ec794b550d5321f1eefa.jpg?s=100&c=85&f=jpeg" data-original="https://media.npr.org/assets/img/2023/10/26/gettyimages-1746298515_sq-6d71bd2abe2eba2a3e85ec794b550d5321f1eefa.jpg?s=100&c=100&f=jpeg" data-template="https://media.npr.org/assets/img/2023/10/26/gettyimages-1746298515_sq-6d71bd2abe2eba2a3e85ec794b550d5321f1eefa.jpg?s={width}&c={quality}&f={format}" data-format="jpeg" class="img lazyOnLoad" type="image/jpeg" /><img src="https://media.npr.org/assets/img/2023/10/26/gettyimages-1746298515_sq-6d71bd2abe2eba2a3e85ec794b550d5321f1eefa.jpg?s=100&c=85&f=jpeg" data-original="https://media.npr.org/assets/img/2023/10/26/gettyimages-1746298515_sq-6d71bd2abe2eba2a3e85ec794b550d5321f1eefa.jpg?s=100&c=100&f=jpeg" data-template="https://media.npr.org/assets/img/2023/10/26/gettyimages-1746298515_sq-6d71bd2abe2eba2a3e85ec794b550d5321f1eefa.jpg?s={width}&c={quality}&f={format}" data-format="jpeg" class="img lazyOnLoad" alt="Israel incursion into Gaza targeted Hamas leaders to prepare for &#039;next stages of war&#039;" loading="lazy" /></picture></a>         <div class="bucketblock">
                        <h3 class="slug"><a href="https://www.npr.org/series/1205445976/middle-east-crisis">Middle East conflict </a></h3>
            <h3><a href="https://www.npr.org/2023/10/26/1208680784/death-toll-in-gaza-approaches-7-000-as-aid-groups-raise-alarm-about-fuel"  data-metrics-ga4='{"category":"recirculation","action":"story_recirculation_click","clickType":"inset box","clickUrl":"https:\/\/www.npr.org\/2023\/10\/26\/1208680784\/death-toll-in-gaza-approaches-7-000-as-aid-groups-raise-alarm-about-fuel"}' >When Israel launched its invasion of Gaza</a></h3>
         </div>

<!-- END CLASS="BUCKETBLOCK" -->
      </div>

<!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" -->
   </div>

<!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-5134606-104" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " -->
   <p>Israel used similar wording about limited raids at the start of its <a href="https://www.npr.org/2023/10/26/1208680784/death-toll-in-gaza-approaches-7-000-as-aid-groups-raise-alarm-about-fuel" target="1208680784">invasion of the Gaza Strip</a> following the Oct. 7 Hamas-led attack on Israel, and the Israeli invasion of Gaza has since expanded and continued to grind on one year later. So Israel's latest comments have raised skepticism in Lebanon about the actual scope of the operation.</p>   <p>“This is not an incursion, this is an invasion,” Najat Aoun Saliba, a Lebanese member of parliament, told NPR. “We've been invaded by another country and we have to call on the international community to call it as such.”</p>   <p>Saliba urged world leaders to call on Israel to put an immediate end to its military offensive in Lebanon.</p>   <aside id="ad-secondary-wrap" class="ad-wrap secondary" aria-label="advertisement">
    <div class="ad-header "><span>Sponsor Message</span></div>

    <div class="ad-config-wrap">
      <div id="ad-secondary-News_World_Middle_East" class="ad-config ad-secondary has-refresh-enabled" data-ad-config='{"network":"\/6735\/","zone":"News_World_Middle_East","targets":{"testserver":"false","isPodcastEpisode":"false","storyId":"nx-s1-5134606","agg":["1205445976","1046346178"]},"site":{"desktop":"NPRSecondary","mobile":"NPRMobileSecondary"},"location":"secondary","deferred":false,"isBetweenContent":true,"hasRefreshEnabled":true,"isOutstreamVideoEnabled":false}'>
        <div style="min-height:90px"></div>
      </div>
    </div>


    <div class="ad-footer "></div>
</aside>
   <p>“We definitely keep saying violence cannot stop violence. We need diplomatic efforts to stop the violence,” Saliba said. “We don't want Lebanon to also turn into another Gaza.”</p>   <p>Israel and Hezbollah began trading attacks back and forth across the Israel-Lebanon border after the Oct. 7 assault on Israel led by the Palestinian militant group Hamas.</p>   <p>In support of Hamas, Hezbollah says it will continue firing rockets into northern Israel until there's a cease-fire in Israel's military campaign in Gaza.</p>
</div>
